#1.Create an empty array to hold all the subsets of the input array.
#2.Determine the size of the power set, which is 2N, where N represents the number of elements in the input array.
#3.Iterate through all possible numbers from 0 to 2N-1: Each number represents a unique combination of elements in the input array.
#4.For each number, generate the corresponding subset.
#5.After constructing each subset, add it to the array of subsets.
#6.Return the array containing all the subsets of the input array.
class Solution:
    def getPowerSet(self, nums):
        n = len(nums)
        subsets = 1 << n
        ans = []
        for num in range(subsets):
            subset = []
            for i in range(n):
                if num & (1 << i):
                    subset.append(nums[i])
            ans.append(subset)
        return ans

